# Deploy to AWS

The project ships Terraform for **AWS ECS Fargate** under `iac/`, driven
entirely by `dude iac …` commands. Architecture:

```
                        ┌────────────────────────────┐
        Internet ──────▶│  ALB (HTTP/HTTPS)          │
                        │   /api/* /admin/*          │
                        │   /django-static/* ────────┼──▶ ECS backend (gunicorn :8000)
                        │   everything else ─────────┼──▶ ECS frontend (nginx :80)
                        └────────────────────────────┘         │
                                                               ▼
                             RDS PostgreSQL ◀── Secrets Manager (DATABASE_URL,
                                                DJANGO_SECRET_KEY)
{{#if withS3}}                             S3 media bucket ◀── django-storages (uploads)
{{/if}}{{#if withRedis}}                             ElastiCache Redis ◀── Celery{{#if withCeleryBeat}} (+ beat){{/if}}
{{/if}}```

Production always runs **PostgreSQL on RDS**, regardless of the local
database choice — `config/settings/production.py` requires `DATABASE_URL`.
Static assets are served by whitenoise from the backend image (collected at
build time); uploads{{#if withS3}} go to the S3 bucket via presigned URLs{{else}} use the default storage{{/if}}.

## Workflow

```bash
dude iac login --env dev
dude iac bootstrap --state-bucket-prefix <your-org> --env dev --yes
dude iac init --env dev
dude iac apply --env dev
dude iac ship --env dev        # build + push + deploy backend & frontend images
dude iac migrate --env dev     # one-off Fargate task: manage.py migrate
```

`dude iac ship` tags both images with the git short SHA (`-dirty` when the
tree has uncommitted changes), records the tag in the environment's
`terraform.tfvars`, and lets ECS roll the services with automatic rollback on
failure.

## Operations

| Task | Command |
| ---- | ------- |
| Service health | `dude iac status --env dev --service backend` |
| Tail logs | `dude iac logs --env dev --service backend --follow` |
| Terraform outputs | `dude iac output --env dev` |
| Preview infra changes | `dude iac plan --env dev` |
| New environment | `dude iac new-env --env staging --from dev` |
| Interactive toolbox | `dude iac shell --env dev` |
| Tear down | `dude iac destroy --env dev` |

See `iac/README.md` for the full reference (custom domains, sizing variables,
state backend details).
